  "prefLabel": "Env-Wt 103.15 Grandfathered structure",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wt 103.15 “Grandfathered structure” means a docking structure that:\n\n(a) Was in place before permit jurisdiction, as defined in Env-Wt 103, took effect;\n\n(b) Has either remained unaltered in location, size, and configuration or is a replacement structure as defined in Env-Wt 104;\n\n(c) Has not been abandoned as defined in Env-Wt 102;\n\n(d) Is consistent with the public’s right to reasonable use of public waters, as established in New Hampshire case law; and\n\n(e) Is not built on land created by the unauthorized filling of public waters.\n\nSource. (See Revision Notes #1, #2, #3, and #4 at Chapter heading for Env-Wt 100) #12801, eff 12-15-19; renumbered by #13945 (formerly Env-Wt 103.14)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wt100.html"
